  "notes": "The melodic half, and the only genuinely diatonic pop writer in this batch: the research says major as often as minor, with I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V families over guitar or pad voicings. So the major families carry the top weights, `session.keys` is majority-major, and `extensions` reaches for sevenths far more than the axis norm. The melody block is where the entry lives — wide ascending leaps into a light falsetto and long sustained tails means `intervals.leap` 0.3, `contour.arch` 0.55, `octaveJumpProb` 0.3, `articulation` `legato`, `register` topping out at 100, and a **low** density band, because the research is explicit that syllable density is low and melodic content is high. That combination appears nowhere else here. The harmonised vocal stacks are `countermelody.densityRatio` 0.6 with `octave_echo` on top — the stack is the lift device, so it doubles rather than answers. ⚠ `confidence` medium (research: high-medium). The INFERRED parameter is `bass808`: \"soft, long 808 or a real bass line; supportive rather than dominant\" gives no figures, so `slideProb` 0.25, `distortion: none` and a register floor of 21 are this author's reading of \"supportive\". ⚠ The verse–pre-chorus–chorus form is authored as a real structure with its own bars and rules, because \"melody-first, chorus early, bridge present\" is a pop form rather than a trap one. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
